{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender account lookup for orders@ shared mailbox missing from Outlook folder list (KB-011 first step)"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and in good standing, so the problem is likely with how the orders@ mailbox is showing in your Outlook. Please try these steps: 1) Fully close Outlook and reopen it. Shared mailboxes are added automatically once access applies, and this can take up to an hour after access is granted. 2) If it still doesn't appear, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com), select Add shared folder or mailbox, and enter orders@. Then let us know whether the orders@ mailbox shows up on the web. Also confirm that your access to orders@ was granted recently, or whether you were already using it before today. If it still doesn't appear after these steps, reply here and we will continue troubleshooting.",
  "internal_note": "Sender James O'Connor (user_id 8, Operations, Warehouse Supervisor, America/Chicago) is active, not locked, not blocked, password not expired, mailbox 29.7% used (no quota issue). Device on record: BL-DT-0108. Tools available cannot verify whether orders@ Send-As or Full Access was granted, so that is unconfirmed. Per KB-011, the next steps are: restart Outlook, check Outlook on the web, then manually add the mailbox. If the user was never granted access, the ticket must go to mailbox owner approval and then Tier 2 under KB-006, which is not yet applicable because access status is unknown. Waiting on user to report restart and OWA results and whether access was recently granted. Note: the user's ticket only says the mailbox 'disappeared', so ask whether it was previously visible.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
